      <h1>Battery Technology</h1>
      <p class="lead">How batteries work — electrochemistry, units, construction and failure modes.</p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> Battery technology is the mechanism layer between the data and the market —
        why a battery has its voltage, why plates are designed the way they are, and how every failure mode
        connects to a construction decision. The deep articles below run on the
        <a href="/technology/how-lead-acid-battery-works/">double-sulfate reaction</a> for lead-acid and on
        intercalation for <a href="/lithium/">lithium</a>.
      </div>

      <h2>What this section covers</h2>
      <p>
        The technology section explains the <strong>mechanisms</strong> — the electrochemical basis, the units
        that quantify it, the construction choices behind each battery type, and the failure modes those
        choices trade off. It is the layer that makes every specification on this site explainable:
        <a href="https://data.worldbatteryhub.com">dimensions and ratings</a> say what; technology says why.
      </p>

